      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Nemotron-Labs-Image-30B-A3B \u00b7 text to image\n\nNVIDIA's autoregressive image model: it writes the image as 16x16-pixel codes, row by row, then the pixel decoder turns the codes into pixels.\n\n**Files** (from [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Nemotron-Labs-Image-ComfyUI)):\n\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| nemotron_labs_image_30b_a3b_w4a8.safetensors (22.7 GB, fits a 24 GB GPU)<br>or `_w4a8_int8dense` (21.6 GB, the fastest), `_w6a8` (30 GB), `_int8_convrot` (36 GB), `_bf16` (65 GB) | `models/diffusion_models/nemotron-image` |\n| nemotron_labs_image_tokenizer_bf16.safetensors | `models/vae/nemotron-image` |\n\n**Settings** (the model card's): temperature 0.9, top_p 1.0, top_k 0. Sizes are multiples of 16; the recommended ones are 1024x1024, 1184x880, 1248x832 and 880x1184. Write the prompt in detail: colours, quantities, text to show, shapes, textures, where things are.\n\n**Memory:** a file that fits the GPU with ~2.5 GB to spare (W4A8 on a 24 GB card) runs there with the pack's kernels; larger ones keep the experts in system RAM with a cache on the GPU (the bf16 file needs about 80 GB of RAM).\n\n**Live preview:** the decoder is also wired into Generate, which decodes the rows written so far every 2 s.\n\nModel: [nvidia/Nemotron-Labs-Image-30B-A3B](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Nemotron-Labs-Image-30B-A3B), NVIDIA License (non-commercial)."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Nemotron-Labs-Image-30B-A3B \u00b7 text to image\n\nNVIDIA's autoregressive image model: it writes the image as 16x16-pixel codes, row by row, then the pixel decoder turns the codes into pixels.\n\n**Files** (from [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Nemotron-Labs-Image-ComfyUI)):\n\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| nemotron_labs_image_30b_a3b_w4a8.safetensors (22.7 GB, fits a 24 GB GPU)<br>or `_w4a8_int8dense` (21.6 GB, the fastest), `_w6a8` (30 GB), `_int8_convrot` (36 GB), `_bf16` (65 GB) | `models/diffusion_models/nemotron-image` |\n| nemotron_labs_image_tokenizer_bf16.safetensors | `models/vae/nemotron-image` |\n\n**Settings** (the model card's): temperature 0.9, top_p 1.0, top_k 0. Sizes are multiples of 16; the recommended ones are 1024x1024, 1184x880, 1248x832 and 880x1184. Write the prompt in detail: colours, quantities, text to show, shapes, textures, where things are.\n\n**Memory:** a file that fits the GPU with ~2.5 GB to spare (W4A8 on a 24 GB card) runs there with the pack's kernels; larger ones keep the experts in system RAM with a cache on the GPU (the bf16 file needs about 80 GB of RAM).\n\n**Live preview:** the decoder is also wired into Generate, which decodes the rows written so far every 2 s.\n\nModel: [nvidia/Nemotron-Labs-Image-30B-A3B](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Nemotron-Labs-Image-30B-A3B), NVIDIA License (non-commercial)."
